IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-4-appeal-812`

-- ccc29-xxviii-7-schedules.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada): the Schedules in lines 17348-17450 of the text: the schedule to Part XX.1 (repealed), the schedule to
-- Part XXII.1 (offences in respect of which a remediation agreement may be entered into), the schedule to Part XXV (section 762: the court, and the officer, for each
-- province or territory) and the schedule to Part XXVII (section 840: fees and allowances). Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a
-- converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text. Every string and amount below was read from the text by
-- work/gen_sched.py, not typed. The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged.

§ `Schedule to Part XX.1`

-- The schedule to Part XX.1 is shown repealed in the text: it has no entries to encode.
-- src:17348 | SCHEDULE TO PART XX.1
-- src:17349 | [Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 37]
@ref Criminal Code sch XX.1 heading to sch XX.1 (src:17348-17349)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch XX.1 the schedule has any entry` MEANS FALSE   -- the text shows "[Repealed, 2005, c. 22, s. 37]" and nothing else

§ `Schedule to Part XXII.1 -- offences in respect of which a remediation agreement may be entered into`

-- The heading says which sections give the schedule effect: section 715.3, subsections 715.32(2) and 715.43(2) and (3). Those sections are outside these sources.
-- The schedule names three groups: (1) offences under listed provisions of this Act; (2) offences under sections 3 and 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act;
-- (3) a conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in 1 or 2.
-- The schedule's own title does not say "only", so an offence it does not name answers NOTHING (fork F-sch-XXII.1).
-- src:17351 | SCHEDULE TO PART XXII.1 (Section 715.3 and subsections 715.32(2) and 715.43(2) and (3)) Offences in respect of which a remediation agreement may be entered into
-- src:17352 | 1 An offence under any of the following provisions of this Act:
-- src:17353 | (a) section 119 or 120 (bribery of officers);
-- src:17354 | (b) section 121 (frauds on the government);
-- src:17355 | (c) section 123 (municipal corruption);
-- src:17356 | (d) section 124 (selling or purchasing office);
-- src:17357 | (e) section 125 (influencing or negotiating appointments or dealing in offices);
-- src:17358 | (f) subsection 139(3) (obstructing justice);
-- src:17359 | (g) section 322 (theft);
-- src:17360 | (h) section 330 (theft by person required to account);
-- src:17361 | (i) section 332 (misappropriation of money held under direction);
-- src:17362 | (j) section 340 (destroying documents of title);
-- src:17363 | (k) section 341 (fraudulent concealment);
-- src:17364 | (l) section 354 (property obtained by crime);
-- src:17365 | (m) section 362 (false pretence or false statement);
-- src:17366 | (n) section 363 (obtaining execution of valuable security by fraud);
-- src:17367 | (o) section 366 (forgery);
-- src:17368 | (p) section 368 (use, trafficking or possession of forged document);
-- src:17369 | (q) section 375 (obtaining by instrument based on forged document);
-- src:17370 | (r) section 378 (offences in relation to registers);
-- src:17371 | (s) section 380 (fraud);
-- src:17372 | (t) section 382 (fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions);
-- src:17373 | (u) section 382.1 (prohibited insider trading);
-- src:17374 | (v) section 383 (gaming in stocks or merchandise);
-- src:17375 | (w) section 389 (fraudulent disposal of goods on which money advanced);
-- src:17376 | (x) section 390 (fraudulent receipts under Bank Act);
-- src:17377 | (x.1) section 391 (trade secret);
-- src:17378 | (y) section 392 (disposal of property to defraud creditors);
-- src:17379 | (z) section 397 (books and documents);
-- src:17380 | (z.1) section 400 (false prospectus);
-- src:17381 | (z.2) section 418 (selling defective stores to Her Majesty); and
-- src:17382 | (z.3) section 426 (secret commissions).
-- src:17383 | (z.4) section 462.31 (laundering proceeds of crime).
@ref Criminal Code sch XXII.1 heading to sch XXII.1 para 1(z.4) (src:17351-17383)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXII.1 para 1 the offence is one of those listed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 119 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 120 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) line 17353
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 121 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b) line 17354
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 123 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (c) line 17355
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 124 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (d) line 17356
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 125 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (e) line 17357
        IF (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 139 AND `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3)") THEN JUST TRUE   -- (f) line 17358
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 322 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g) line 17359
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 330 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (h) line 17360
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 332 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (i) line 17361
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 340 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (j) line 17362
