-- src:17384 | 2 An offence under any of the following provisions of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act:
-- src:17385 | a) section 3 (bribing a foreign public official); and
-- src:17386 | b) section 4 (maintenance or destruction of books and records to facilitate or hide the bribing of a foreign public official).
-- src:17387 | 3 A conspiracy or an attempt to commit, being an accessory after the fact in relation to, or any counselling in relation to, an offence referred to in section 1 or 2.
@ref Criminal Code sch XXII.1 heading to sch XXII.1 para 3 (src:17351-17387)
DECLARE `sch XXII.1 offence` HAS
    `the provision under which the offence is charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `it is an offence under section 3 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an offence under section 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Criminal Code sch XXII.1 heading to sch XXII.1 para 3 (src:17351-17387)
GIVEN offence IS A `sch XXII.1 offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXII.1 the offence is listed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sch XXII.1 para 1 the offence is one of those listed` (offence's `the provision under which the offence is charged`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `sch XXII.1 para 2 the offence is one of those listed` (offence's `it is an offence under section 3 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`) (offence's `it is an offence under section 4 of the Corruption of Foreign Public Officials Act`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the schedule lists provisions and does not say that no other offence is covered

§ `Schedule to Part XXV (section 762)`

-- Column I names the province or territory, Column II the court, and Column III the officer. A row with no entry in Column I continues the one above.
-- src:17389 | SCHEDULE [to Part XXV] (Section 762)
-- src:17390 | Column I | Column II | Column III
-- src:17391 | Ontario | A judge of the Court of Appeal in respect of a release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before the Court | The Registrar of the Court of Appeal
-- src:17392 | The Superior Court of Justice in respect of undertakings or all other release orders or recognizances | A Registrar of the Superior Court of Justice
-- src:17393 | Quebec | The Court of Quebec, Criminal and Penal Division | The Clerk of the Court
-- src:17394 | Nova Scotia | The Supreme Court | A Prothonotary of the Supreme Court
-- src:17395 | New Brunswick | The Court of Queen’s Bench | The Registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench
-- src:17396 | British Columbia | The Supreme Court in respect of an undertaking, release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before that Court or the Court of Appeal | The District Registrar of the Supreme Court
-- src:17397 | A Provincial Court in respect of an undertaking, release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before a judge of that Court or a justice | The Clerk of the Provincial Court
-- src:17398 | Prince Edward Island | The Supreme Court | The Prothonotary
-- src:17399 | Manitoba | The Court of Queen’s Bench | The registrar or a deputy registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench
-- src:17400 | Saskatchewan | The Court of Queen’s Bench | The Local Registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench
-- src:17401 | Alberta | The Court of Queen’s Bench | The Clerk of the Court of Queen’s Bench
-- src:17402 | Newfoundland and Labrador | The Supreme Court | The Registrar of the Supreme Court
-- src:17403 | Yukon | The Supreme Court | The Clerk of the Supreme Court
-- src:17404 | Northwest Territories | The Supreme Court | The Clerk of the Supreme Court
-- src:17405 | Nunavut | The Nunavut Court of Justice | The Clerk of the Nunavut Court of Justice
@ref Criminal Code sch XXV heading to sch XXV Nunavut row 1 (src:17389-17405)
DECLARE `sch XXV row` IS ONE OF
    `sch XXV Ontario row 1`
    `sch XXV Ontario row 2`
    `sch XXV Quebec row 1`
    `sch XXV Nova Scotia row 1`
    `sch XXV New Brunswick row 1`
    `sch XXV British Columbia row 1`
    `sch XXV British Columbia row 2`
    `sch XXV Prince Edward Island row 1`
    `sch XXV Manitoba row 1`
    `sch XXV Saskatchewan row 1`
    `sch XXV Alberta row 1`
    `sch XXV Newfoundland and Labrador row 1`
    `sch XXV Yukon row 1`
    `sch XXV Northwest Territories row 1`
    `sch XXV Nunavut row 1`

@ref Criminal Code sch XXV heading to sch XXV Nunavut row 1 (src:17389-17405)
GIVEN row IS A `sch XXV row`
GIVETH A `s 812(1) province or territory`
`sch XXV column I the province or territory of the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Ontario`
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 2` THEN `s 812(1) Ontario`
    WHEN `sch XXV Quebec row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Quebec`
    WHEN `sch XXV Nova Scotia row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Nova Scotia`
    WHEN `sch XXV New Brunswick row 1` THEN `s 812(1) New Brunswick`
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 1` THEN `s 812(1) British Columbia`
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 2` THEN `s 812(1) British Columbia`
    WHEN `sch XXV Prince Edward Island row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Prince Edward Island`
    WHEN `sch XXV Manitoba row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Manitoba`
    WHEN `sch XXV Saskatchewan row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Saskatchewan`
    WHEN `sch XXV Alberta row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Alberta`
    WHEN `sch XXV Newfoundland and Labrador row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador`
    WHEN `sch XXV Yukon row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Yukon`
    WHEN `sch XXV Northwest Territories row 1` THEN `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories`
    WHEN `sch XXV Nunavut row 1` THEN `s 812(1) Nunavut`

@ref Criminal Code sch XXV heading to sch XXV Nunavut row 1 (src:17389-17405)
GIVEN row IS A `sch XXV row`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch XXV column II the court of the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 1` THEN "A judge of the Court of Appeal in respect of a release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before the Court"   -- line 17391
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 2` THEN "The Superior Court of Justice in respect of undertakings or all other release orders or recognizances"   -- line 17392
    WHEN `sch XXV Quebec row 1` THEN "The Court of Quebec, Criminal and Penal Division"   -- line 17393
    WHEN `sch XXV Nova Scotia row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court"   -- line 17394
    WHEN `sch XXV New Brunswick row 1` THEN "The Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17395
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court in respect of an undertaking, release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before that Court or the Court of Appeal"   -- line 17396
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 2` THEN "A Provincial Court in respect of an undertaking, release order or recognizance for the appearance of a person before a judge of that Court or a justice"   -- line 17397
    WHEN `sch XXV Prince Edward Island row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court"   -- line 17398
    WHEN `sch XXV Manitoba row 1` THEN "The Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17399
    WHEN `sch XXV Saskatchewan row 1` THEN "The Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17400
    WHEN `sch XXV Alberta row 1` THEN "The Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17401
    WHEN `sch XXV Newfoundland and Labrador row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court"   -- line 17402
    WHEN `sch XXV Yukon row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court"   -- line 17403
    WHEN `sch XXV Northwest Territories row 1` THEN "The Supreme Court"   -- line 17404
    WHEN `sch XXV Nunavut row 1` THEN "The Nunavut Court of Justice"   -- line 17405

@ref Criminal Code sch XXV heading to sch XXV Nunavut row 1 (src:17389-17405)
GIVEN row IS A `sch XXV row`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch XXV column III the officer of the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 1` THEN "The Registrar of the Court of Appeal"   -- line 17391
    WHEN `sch XXV Ontario row 2` THEN "A Registrar of the Superior Court of Justice"   -- line 17392
    WHEN `sch XXV Quebec row 1` THEN "The Clerk of the Court"   -- line 17393
    WHEN `sch XXV Nova Scotia row 1` THEN "A Prothonotary of the Supreme Court"   -- line 17394
    WHEN `sch XXV New Brunswick row 1` THEN "The Registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17395
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 1` THEN "The District Registrar of the Supreme Court"   -- line 17396
    WHEN `sch XXV British Columbia row 2` THEN "The Clerk of the Provincial Court"   -- line 17397
    WHEN `sch XXV Prince Edward Island row 1` THEN "The Prothonotary"   -- line 17398
    WHEN `sch XXV Manitoba row 1` THEN "The registrar or a deputy registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17399
    WHEN `sch XXV Saskatchewan row 1` THEN "The Local Registrar of the Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17400
    WHEN `sch XXV Alberta row 1` THEN "The Clerk of the Court of Queen’s Bench"   -- line 17401
    WHEN `sch XXV Newfoundland and Labrador row 1` THEN "The Registrar of the Supreme Court"   -- line 17402
    WHEN `sch XXV Yukon row 1` THEN "The Clerk of the Supreme Court"   -- line 17403
    WHEN `sch XXV Northwest Territories row 1` THEN "The Clerk of the Supreme Court"   -- line 17404
    WHEN `sch XXV Nunavut row 1` THEN "The Clerk of the Nunavut Court of Justice"   -- line 17405

@ref Criminal Code sch XXV heading to sch XXV Nunavut row 1 (src:17389-17405)
GIVEN place IS A `s 812(1) province or territory`
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch XXV row`
`sch XXV the rows of the province or territory` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `s 812(1) Ontario` THEN LIST `sch XXV Ontario row 1`, `sch XXV Ontario row 2`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Quebec` THEN LIST `sch XXV Quebec row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nova Scotia` THEN LIST `sch XXV Nova Scotia row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) New Brunswick` THEN LIST `sch XXV New Brunswick row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) British Columbia` THEN LIST `sch XXV British Columbia row 1`, `sch XXV British Columbia row 2`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Prince Edward Island` THEN LIST `sch XXV Prince Edward Island row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Manitoba` THEN LIST `sch XXV Manitoba row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Saskatchewan` THEN LIST `sch XXV Saskatchewan row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Alberta` THEN LIST `sch XXV Alberta row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN LIST `sch XXV Newfoundland and Labrador row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Yukon` THEN LIST `sch XXV Yukon row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories` THEN LIST `sch XXV Northwest Territories row 1`
    WHEN `s 812(1) Nunavut` THEN LIST `sch XXV Nunavut row 1`

§ `Schedule to Part XXVII (section 840): fees and allowances`

-- The table gives each item's words and amount. The amount is the figure in the row. Its unit (a flat amount, each mile, each day, and so on) is read from the row's own words.
-- Items 3 and 4 carry the same words ("Warrant where summons issued in first instance $ 0.30") in the text; both are encoded as written (finding).
-- Items 11 states no amount of its own: it says each justice "is entitled to the fee authorized by item 9". The note lines in parentheses are encoded after the table, each as its own function.
-- src:17407 | SCHEDULE [to Part XXVII] (Section 840)
-- src:17409 | Fees and Allowances That May Be Charged by Summary Conviction Courts and Justices
-- src:17410 | 1 Information $ 1.00
-- src:17411 | 2 Summons or warrant $ 0.50
-- src:17412 | 3 Warrant where summons issued in first instance $ 0.30
-- src:17413 | 4 Warrant where summons issued in first instance $ 0.30
-- src:17414 | 5 Each subpoena or warrant to or for witnesses $ 0.30
-- src:17415 | (A subpoena may contain any number of names. Only one subpoena may be issued on behalf of a party in any proceeding, unless the summary conviction court or the justice considers it necessary or desirable that more than one subpoena be issued.)
-- src:17416 | 6 Information for warrant for witness and warrant for witness $ 1.00
-- src:17417 | 7 Each necessary copy of subpoena to or warrant for witness $ 0.20
-- src:17418 | 8 Each release order or recognizance $ 1.00
-- src:17419 | 9 Hearing and determining proceeding $ 1.00
-- src:17420 | 10 Where hearing lasts more than two hours $ 2.00
-- src:17421 | 11 Where two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding, each is entitled to the fee authorized by item 9.
-- src:17422 | 12 Each warrant of committal $ 0.50
-- src:17423 | 13 Making up record of conviction or order on request of a party to the proceedings $ 1.00
-- src:17424 | 14 Copy of a writing other than a conviction or order, on request of a party to the proceedings; for each folio of one hundred words $ 0.10
-- src:17425 | 15 Bill of costs, when made out in detail on request of a party to the proceedings $ 0.20
-- src:17426 | (Items 14 and 15 may be charged only where there has been an adjudication.)
-- src:17427 | 16 Attending to remand prisoner $ 1.00
-- src:17428 | 17 Attending to make a release order or take a recognizance $ 1.00
-- src:17430 | Fees and Allowances That May Be Allowed to Peace Officers
-- src:17431 | 18 Arresting a person on a warrant or without a warrant $ 1.50
-- src:17432 | 19 Serving summons or subpoena $ 0.50
-- src:17433 | 20 Mileage to serve summons or subpoena or to make an arrest, both ways, for each mile $ 0.10
-- src:17434 | (Where a public conveyance is not used, reasonable costs of transportation may be allowed.)
-- src:17435 | 21 Mileage where service cannot be effected, on proof of a diligent attempt to effect service, each way, for each mile $ 0.10
-- src:17436 | 22 Returning with prisoner after arrest to take him before a summary conviction court or justice at a place different from the place where the peace officer received the warrant to arrest, if the journey is of necessity over a route different from that taken by the peace officer to make the arrest, each way, for each mile $ 0.10
-- src:17437 | 23 Taking a prisoner to prison on remand or committal, each way, for each mile $ 0.10
-- src:17438 | (Where a public conveyance is not used, reasonable costs of transportation may be allowed. No charge may be made under this item in respect of a service for which a charge is made under item 22.)
-- src:17439 | 24 Attending summary conviction court or justice on summary conviction proceedings, for each day necessarily employed $ 2.00
-- src:17440 | (Not more than $2.00 may be charged under this item in respect of any day notwithstanding the number of proceedings that the peace officer attended on that day before that summary conviction court or justice.)
-- src:17442 | Fees and Allowances That May Be Allowed to Witnesses
-- src:17443 | 25 Each day attending trial $ 4.00
-- src:17444 | 26 Mileage travelled to attend trial, each way, for each mile $ 0.10
-- src:17446 | Fees and Allowances That May Be Allowed to Interpreters
-- src:17447 | 27 Each half day attending trial $ 2.50
-- src:17448 | 28 Actual living expenses when away from ordinary place of residence, not to exceed per day $ 10.00
-- src:17449 | 29 Mileage travelled to attend trial, each way, for each mile $ 0.10
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII heading to sch XXVII item 29 (src:17407-17449)
DECLARE `sch XXVII payee group` IS ONE OF
    `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be charged by summary conviction courts and justices`
    `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to peace officers`
    `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to witnesses`
    `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to interpreters`

DECLARE `sch XXVII unit` IS ONE OF
    `sch XXVII a flat amount`
    `sch XXVII for each folio of one hundred words`
    `sch XXVII for each mile`
    `sch XXVII for each day`
    `sch XXVII for each half day`
    `sch XXVII not to exceed per day`

@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII heading to sch XXVII item 29 (src:17407-17449)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch XXVII the amount in dollars stated in the row of the item` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17410
        IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 0.50   -- line 17411
        IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 0.30   -- line 17412
        IF item EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 0.30   -- line 17413
        IF item EQUALS 5 THEN JUST 0.30   -- line 17414
        IF item EQUALS 6 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17416
        IF item EQUALS 7 THEN JUST 0.20   -- line 17417
        IF item EQUALS 8 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17418
        IF item EQUALS 9 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17419
        IF item EQUALS 10 THEN JUST 2.00   -- line 17420
        IF item EQUALS 11 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): line 17421 states no amount of its own; it refers to "the fee authorized by item 9"
        IF item EQUALS 12 THEN JUST 0.50   -- line 17422
        IF item EQUALS 13 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17423
        IF item EQUALS 14 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17424
        IF item EQUALS 15 THEN JUST 0.20   -- line 17425
        IF item EQUALS 16 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17427
        IF item EQUALS 17 THEN JUST 1.00   -- line 17428
        IF item EQUALS 18 THEN JUST 1.50   -- line 17431
        IF item EQUALS 19 THEN JUST 0.50   -- line 17432
        IF item EQUALS 20 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17433
        IF item EQUALS 21 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17435
        IF item EQUALS 22 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17436
        IF item EQUALS 23 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17437
        IF item EQUALS 24 THEN JUST 2.00   -- line 17439
        IF item EQUALS 25 THEN JUST 4.00   -- line 17443
        IF item EQUALS 26 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17444
        IF item EQUALS 27 THEN JUST 2.50   -- line 17447
        IF item EQUALS 28 THEN JUST 10.00   -- line 17448
        IF item EQUALS 29 THEN JUST 0.10   -- line 17449
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the schedule has items 1 to 29

