@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII heading to sch XXVII item 29 (src:17407-17449)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `sch XXVII payee group`
`sch XXVII the group under which the item stands` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF item AT LEAST 1 AND item AT MOST 17 THEN JUST `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be charged by summary conviction courts and justices`   -- heading at line 17409
        IF item AT LEAST 18 AND item AT MOST 24 THEN JUST `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to peace officers`   -- heading at line 17430
        IF item AT LEAST 25 AND item AT MOST 26 THEN JUST `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to witnesses`   -- heading at line 17442
        IF item AT LEAST 27 AND item AT MOST 29 THEN JUST `sch XXVII fees and allowances that may be allowed to interpreters`   -- heading at line 17446
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the schedule has items 1 to 29

-- Item 5 note: the subpoena. "A subpoena may contain any number of names" is the first sentence; the second bars a second subpoena for a party unless the court or justice considers it necessary or desirable.
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 5 (src:17415)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, gate closed by the text: "Only one subpoena may be issued ... unless the summary conviction court or the justice considers it necessary or desirable"
GIVEN `one subpoena has already been issued on behalf of the party in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary conviction court or the justice considers it necessary or desirable that more than one subpoena be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 5 a further subpoena may be issued on behalf of the party in the proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `one subpoena has already been issued on behalf of the party in the proceeding` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "Only one subpoena may be issued on behalf of a party in any proceeding": the first is allowed
        IF `the summary conviction court or the justice considers it necessary or desirable that more than one subpoena be issued` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "unless the summary conviction court or the justice considers it necessary or desirable"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only one subpoena may be issued on behalf of a party in any proceeding, unless ..."

@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 5 (src:17415)
-- @name-test: no JUST FALSE branch; named for a power, answers NOTHING outside "any number of names"
GIVEN `the number of names in the subpoena` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 5 the subpoena may contain the number of names` MEANS
    IF `the number of names in the subpoena` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "A subpoena may contain any number of names"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any number of names" says nothing of a subpoena with no name

-- Item 10: "Where hearing lasts more than two hours $ 2.00".
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII item 10 (src:17420)
GIVEN `the hearing lasts more than two hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII item 10 the fee applies` MEANS
    IF `the hearing lasts more than two hours`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where hearing lasts more than two hours"

-- Item 11: "Where two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding, each is entitled to the fee authorized by item 9."
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII item 11 (src:17421)
-- @name-test: listed, "entitled" and a where-kind gate (F-sch-XXVII-11): "Where two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII item 11 each justice is entitled to the fee authorized by item 9` MEANS
    IF `two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where two or more justices hear and determine a proceeding"

-- Item 15 note: "Items 14 and 15 may be charged only where there has been an adjudication."
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 15 (src:17426)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, gate closed by the text: "may be charged only where there has been an adjudication"
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
      `there has been an adjudication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 15 the item may be charged` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS 14 OR item EQUALS 15
    THEN IF `there has been an adjudication`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Items 14 and 15 may be charged only where there has been an adjudication"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the note speaks of items 14 and 15 only

-- Item 20 note and item 23 note: "Where a public conveyance is not used, reasonable costs of transportation may be allowed."
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 20 (src:17434)
-- @name-test: listed, where-kind (F-sch-XXVII-20): "Where a public conveyance is not used" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
      `a public conveyance is not used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 20 reasonable costs of transportation may be allowed` MEANS
    IF item EQUALS 20 OR item EQUALS 23
    THEN IF `a public conveyance is not used`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a public conveyance is not used"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the notes after items 20 and 23 speak of those items only

-- Item 23 note, second sentence: "No charge may be made under this item in respect of a service for which a charge is made under item 22."
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 23 (src:17438)
-- @name-test: kept JUST FALSE, a flat negative: "No charge may be made under this item in respect of a service for which a charge is made under item 22"
GIVEN `a charge is made under item 22 for the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 23 a charge may be made under item 23 in respect of the service` MEANS
    IF `a charge is made under item 22 for the service`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No charge may be made under this item in respect of a service for which a charge is made under item 22"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the note says nothing of a service for which no charge is made under item 22

-- Item 22: the journey condition is part of the row: "if the journey is of necessity over a route different from that taken by the peace officer to make the arrest".
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII item 22 (src:17436)
GIVEN `the journey is of necessity over a route different from that taken by the peace officer to make the arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII item 22 the fee applies` MEANS
    IF `the journey is of necessity over a route different from that taken by the peace officer to make the arrest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the journey is of necessity over a route different from that taken by the peace officer to make the arrest"

-- Item 24 note: "Not more than $2.00 may be charged under this item in respect of any day notwithstanding the number of proceedings ..."
@ref Criminal Code sch XXVII note after item 24 (src:17440)
GIVEN `the amount in dollars charged under item 24 in respect of the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch XXVII note after item 24 the amount charged for the day is within the limit` MEANS
    `the amount in dollars charged under item 24 in respect of the day` AT MOST 2.00   -- "Not more than $2.00 may be charged under this item in respect of any day": a stated maximum
